    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Daulton Varsho** (69.56) headlines our lineup as the most efficient start, leveraging a high-ceiling matchup against M\u00e1rquez (5.58 xERA) to maximize power-speed upside. He is closely followed by our trio of top-tier plays in **Taylor Ward** (68.88), **Dylan Beavers** (68.38), and **Luis Arraez** (65.86). The offensive environment for **Taylor Ward** and **Dylan Beavers** is particularly optimized by their matchup against Lugo, benefiting from park factors that elevate their run-production potential. Meanwhile, **Luis Arraez** thrives today on an elite 18% skill-boost against the middling arm of Lorenzen; his ability to stabilize our AVG category while benefiting from a favorable batting order position makes him a cornerstone of the LawDog rotation for this matchup.\n\nOur most difficult benching decision involved **Bryce Harper**, who remains a high-variance asset despite his 50.42 score. While his elite xwOBA of 0.394 usually warrants a spot, the 2.69 xERA of his opposing starter, Skubal, creates a structural efficiency floor that forced us to favor more favorable matchups, such as **Jung Hoo Lee** (62.57) and **Jonathan Aranda** (55.23). Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the speed profiles of our active roster; while **Tyler Freeman** (49.94) draws a tougher matchup, his presence in the lineup is justified by his ability to exploit McDonald\u2019s slow delivery for stolen base opportunities, a critical factor given the scarcity of speed in our current build. \n\nRisks today are largely concentrated on the fringe of the order. **Cal Raleigh** (52.07) and **Lawrence Butler** (54.37) carry the highest volatility; **Cal Raleigh** must contend with an efficient southpaw in Seymour, while **Lawrence Butler** faces a significant platoon disadvantage against Schultz. We will keep a close eye on weather developments, but as it stands, this configuration maximizes our expected value across the 5x5 categories while maintaining enough bench depth\u2014led by **Drew Gilbert** and **Gavin Sheets**\u2014to pivot if late-breaking lineup changes impact our order-based efficiency bonuses.",
